+/**
+ * Paper’s chunk-system rewrite (Moonrise / “chunk system”) targets the same goals as the Fabric mod
+ * <a href="https://github.com/RelativityMC/C2ME-fabric">C2ME</a> (Concurrent Chunk Management Engine):
+ * scale chunk generation, loading, and region I/O across CPU cores with explicit schedulers and priority queues.
+ * <p>
+ * C2ME wraps vanilla’s {@code ServerChunkManager} with mixins (e.g. priority scheduling, consolidated level updates).
+ * Tentacles uses this stack instead: {@link ca.spottedleaf.moonrise.patches.chunk_system.scheduling.ChunkTaskScheduler}
+ * owns parallel generation, load, compression, save, and I/O executors; ticket propagation is handled by
+ * {@link ca.spottedleaf.moonrise.patches.chunk_system.scheduling.ChunkHolderManager} and
+ * {@link ca.spottedleaf.moonrise.patches.chunk_system.scheduling.ThreadedTicketLevelPropagator}.
+ * <p>
+ * Thread pool sizes and global limits remain in Paper’s configuration (e.g. {@code paper-global.yml}), analogous to
+ * C2ME’s module parallelism settings. Tentacles additionally uses a finer {@link ca.spottedleaf.concurrentutil.executor.queue.AreaDependentQueue}
+ * grid for generation and thread-local scratch lists in {@link ca.spottedleaf.moonrise.patches.chunk_system.scheduling.ChunkHolderManager}
+ * to reduce allocation churn during ticket updates.
+ */
+@org.jspecify.annotations.NullMarked
+package ca.spottedleaf.moonrise.patches.chunk_system;
